    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class with `@Test`, and it passes. The full build succeeds.\n\nThe change is complete. Here's what I implemented, following the existing `customerCode` conventions:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `membershipNumber` field (`@Column(name = \"membership_number\")`) with getter/setter, mirroring `customerCode`.\n\n2. **`MembershipNumberGenerator.java`** (new, in `rest/validation/`) \u2014 a stateless utility mirroring `CustomerCodeGenerator`, with a single responsibility: format `<customerCode>-M<YY>` where `YY` is the zero-padded last two digits of the registration year (`String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", customerCode, registrationDate.getYear() % 100)`).\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 assigns `membershipNumber` right after `saveOwner`. Placing it post-save means the entity's `@PrePersist` default has already populated `registrationDate` (when the client omits it), so the generator always sees a non-null date that exactly matches the persisted/returned value \u2014 no duplication of the defaulting logic.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `membershipNumber` as a `readOnly` string to the `Owner` schema, so MapStruct's `OwnerMapper` maps it by name into the response DTO automatically (no mapper change needed).\n\n5. **Schema DDL** \u2014 added a `membership_number` column to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres), since `ddl-auto=none` for the test profile means the column must exist explicitly.\n\nResult: `SMI-0007` registered in 2026 \u2192 `SMI-0007-M26`. Test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, including the `coreMembershipNumberFormat` acceptance test).",
